    <string name="rationale_title">PulseStages and your health data</string>
    <string name="rationale_intro">PulseStages estimates sleep stages from data in Health Connect. This page lists what it reads and writes and how to delete its data. It is also the privacy policy that Health Connect shows.</string>
    <string name="rationale_bullet">•</string>
    <string name="rationale_read_title">What is read</string>
    <string name="rationale_read_sleep">Sleep sessions of the apps you select (by default OHealth), to know when you slept.</string>
    <string name="rationale_read_heart_rate">Heart rate during and around each night — the main signal of the estimate.</string>
    <string name="rationale_read_steps">Steps, as a measure of movement during the night.</string>
    <string name="rationale_read_optional">Optionally blood oxygen (SpO2), respiratory rate and heart-rate variability, when they exist and you allow them.</string>
    <string name="rationale_read_history">Access to data older than 30 days before PulseStages was first given access, to estimate past nights when you start a backfill.</string>
    <string name="rationale_read_background">Background access, so that new nights are estimated automatically while the app is closed.</string>
    <string name="rationale_write_title">What is written</string>
    <string name="rationale_write_sessions">Its own sleep sessions with the estimated stages (awake, light, deep, REM), marked as an estimate with the algorithm version.</string>
    <string name="rationale_write_never_others">It never changes or deletes data of other apps; Health Connect does not allow it.</string>
    <string name="rationale_device_title">Nothing leaves your device</string>
    <string name="rationale_device_no_internet">PulseStages has no internet permission: it cannot send your data anywhere.</string>
    <string name="rationale_device_local">All processing happens on the phone. Its own records (settings, log, which nights were estimated) stay in the app\'s private storage.</string>
    <string name="rationale_device_saa_request">With “Ask Sleep as Android to sync” (on by default; Settings → Written sessions), once a night it wrote is complete, it asks Sleep as Android, if installed, to sync with Health Connect. The request carries no data.</string>
    <string name="rationale_delete_title">How to delete its data</string>
    <string name="rationale_delete_in_app">In the app: Home → “Delete my sessions from Health Connect” removes every session PulseStages wrote.</string>
    <string name="rationale_delete_health_connect">In Health Connect: App permissions → PulseStages → Delete app data; there you can also revoke every permission.</string>
    <string name="rationale_delete_uninstall">Uninstalling PulseStages deletes its private storage and revokes its permissions.</string>
